      "problem": "Factor $1 - \\dfrac 1 {t^9}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\na^3-b^3=(a-b)(a^2+ab+b^2).\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n1 - \\dfrac{1}{t^9}  = 1^3 - \\left( \\dfrac{1}{t^3}\\right)^3\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{9}} & ={1}^{3}-{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}})}^{3} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}})({1}^{2}+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}})}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}})(1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{({t}^{3})^{2}}) \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}})(1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{6}})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
